# Diagnostics for the in-stadium screens (the "jumbotron").
#
# The screens are model packets carrying object-creation flag bit 16.
# DrawableModel swaps Jumbotron::m_CurrentTexture onto texmap 0 for those
# packets, and Jumbotron plays a 16-frame animation loaded from
# jumbotron/{kickoff,goal,wins}.glt into one fixed buffer.
#
# Nothing here changes what the game renders unless a switch is set:
#
#   OPENSTRIKERS_JUMBO_DEBUG=1  traces the state machine (the four presentation
#       opcodes 5/13/25/28 that drive it, the frame the game selected, and the
#       first bytes actually sitting in the frame's buffer), plus per-frame
#       counts of how many flagged models were submitted, how many reached the
#       packet loop, how many took the animation texture, and -- when one did
#       not -- which early return in DrawModel ate it.
#
#   OPENSTRIKERS_JUMBO_FORCE=1  keeps every flagged surface opaque and hands it
#       a known-good frame, so a capture shows where the screens actually are.
#       This is how they were located: they are the wide panels set into the
#       stadium wall below the crowd, at both ends of the pitch.
#
# Note that the screens are deliberately transparent in the gameplay camera
# (World.cpp DoTranslucency hides creation flags 0x2000/0x8000 there), so
# "not drawn during play" is correct behaviour, not a fault.
#
# This patch also folds in the SKYDROP diagnostic from the earlier skybox
# investigation, which was sitting unsaved in the working tree and would
# otherwise have been lost the next time the stack was re-applied.
